275
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,600
This is so great. Did you hear that?

276
00:12:06,650 --> 00:12:08,260
Yeah, I did.

277
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,420
Hey.

278
00:12:09,970 --> 00:12:13,180
Thank you. Thank you so much.

279
00:12:15,090 --> 00:12:17,140
You are so going to heaven!

280
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,920
We got some really great stuff.

281
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,130
Yeah.

282
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:29,820
Yeah, but I'm not sure about some of the bras I got.

283
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:32,230
Really? Do you want to try some of them on for me?

284
00:12:32,230 --> 00:12:33,500
Okay.

285
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,690
Wait, are we in Joey's imagination?

286
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:42,690
Oh, no. I took one of Ross' bags by mistake.

287
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:44,320
And one of mine is missing.

288
00:12:44,370 --> 00:12:45,750
Ross probably has it.

289
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,340
You'll get it from him later.

290
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:55,680
So, what do you think?

291
00:12:58,270 --> 00:13:01,080
I think we're not wearing the same shirt anymore.

292
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:05,000
Yeah. Yeah, Rachel picked it out for me.

293
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,520
She told me to trust her, and you know what?

294
00:13:06,570 --> 00:13:07,790
I'm glad I did.

295
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:10,240
I turned quite a few heads on my way over here.

296
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:15,380
Dude, I really don't think you should be wearing that.

297
00:13:16,330 --> 00:13:17,890
I see.

298
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:21,440
Somebody's afraid of a little competition with the ladies?

299
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:25,050
Looks like someone is the ladies!

300
00:13:26,510 --> 00:13:29,320
You're just jealous because you couldn't pull this off.

301
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:33,070
Yeah. Now if you'll excuse me, I have a date.

302
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:38,620
See? All eyes on me!

303
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:46,460
We are not signing those papers.

304
00:13:46,510 --> 00:13:47,850
Why not?

305
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:50,390
It's wrong. They made a mistake.

306
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,790
They think we're somebody else.

307
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,210
God works in mysterious ways.

308
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,780
You have got to stop.

309
00:13:57,570 --> 00:13:59,460
But she liked us.

310
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:01,110
She likes Doctor Chandler

311
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,470
and Reverend Monica.

312
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,350
If you think about it,

313
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,130
I'm kind of like a reverend.

314
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:09,890
I mean, as a chef, I serve God

315
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:12,840
by feeding the hungry and poor.

316
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,410
Your veal chop is 34.95!

317
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:18,860
Come on,

318
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:20,980
I just-- I think we've been given an opportunity.

319
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:22,570
The mistake's already made.

320
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:24,160
They're writing up the papers now.

321
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:26,120
But we're not the ones she chose.

322
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:28,530
How can you feel okay about this?

323
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:31,460
Because.

324
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:35,330
We may not be who she thinks we are...

325
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:38,160
...but no one will ever love that baby more than us.

326
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,260
- I know.  - I mean, who knows...

327
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:41,750
...how long it's gonna take for someone else

328
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,300
to give us a baby?

329
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:46,000
What if no one ever picks us?

330
00:14:46,050 --> 00:14:47,630
Oh, honey....

331
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,310
Please?

332
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:51,980
Please. We are so close.

333
00:14:54,090 --> 00:14:56,050
Monica, I want a baby too.

334
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,970
But this woman is giving away her child.

335
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,850
She deserves to know who it's going to.

336
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:11,040
Okay. You're right.

337
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:15,850
So we'll tell the truth.

338
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,030
And who knows, you know?

339
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,960
Maybe she'll like us for us.

340
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:23,410
Maybe she will.

341
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,720
Why couldn't I have been a reverend?

342
00:15:26,770 --> 00:15:28,220
You're Jewish.

343
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,000
Technicality!

344
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:39,920
Garden salad for the lady.

345
00:15:39,970 --> 00:15:42,350
Oh, that looks great. Good ordering.

346
00:15:43,110 --> 00:15:45,760
Seafood platter for the gentleman,

347
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,350
and extra fries.

348
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,600
Enjoy.

349
00:15:51,330 --> 00:15:53,000
Those fries look delicious.

350
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,670
I didn't know you liked French fries.

351
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,140
Help yourself. What's mine is yours.

352
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:05,050
Wow, are those stuffed clams?

353
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,870
Yes, they are my stuffed clams.

354
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,090
How about those fries, though, huh?

355
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:20,770
- They are delicious.  - Yeah.

356
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:27,060
You are beautiful, you know that?

357
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:30,780
That is so sweet.

358
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:34,120
Okay, then.

359
00:16:45,910 --> 00:16:47,730
Now look what you did!

360
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:50,450
What? What is the matter with you?

361
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:51,680
I don't like it

362
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:54,540
when people take food off of my plate, okay?

363
00:16:54,590 --> 00:16:56,430
But you said, "What's mine is yours."

364
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,050
Well, I didn't mean it!

365
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:01,470
Fine. Sorry,

366
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,800
I didn't think it was that big a deal.

367
00:17:05,490 --> 00:17:07,310
No, I'm sorry. I....

368
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,640
I'm overreacting, okay?

369
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:12,240
It's just, when it comes to food, l...

370
00:17:12,290 --> 00:17:13,640
...have certain rules...

371
00:17:13,650 --> 00:17:15,470
...okay? I mean...

372
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,480
...there are things you do,

373
00:17:17,530 --> 00:17:20,440
and, you know, things that you don't do.

374
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,630
Wow, this place looks great.

375
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,040
Oh, you are gonna love it.

376
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:34,290
And I'm so glad we're finally doing this.

377
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:36,780
- Me too.  - Here.

378
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:47,400
So this was fun.

379
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:58,950
I really am sorry about, you know, before.

380
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,750
And I want to make sure you know

381
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,200
I really do like you.

382
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:05,170
Sure, just not as much as clams.

383
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,870
Well, stuffed clams....

384
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,940
Chocolate torte for the lady.

385
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:13,020
Cheesecake for the gentleman.

386
00:18:13,070 --> 00:18:14,530
Excuse me, sir.

387
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:17,600
There seems to be some sort of red crap on my cheesecake.

388
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:21,570
Yes, that's a raspberry coulis.

389
00:18:21,570 --> 00:18:23,270
I'm so stupid ordering cheesecake,

390
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:24,890
trying to be healthy.

391
00:18:38,030 --> 00:18:39,940
Oh, no.

392
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:42,080
This is work. I should call in.

393
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:43,420
Can you excuse me?

394
00:18:43,470 --> 00:18:45,380
Yeah, sure. No problem.

395
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,070
What are you doing?

396
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,300
I thought you don't share food?

397
00:18:51,350 --> 00:18:52,780
Sure I do.

398
00:18:52,830 --> 00:18:54,110
Coulis?

399
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:58,040
No. If I can't have your clams,

400
00:18:58,090 --> 00:18:59,320
you can't have my dessert.

401
00:18:59,370 --> 00:19:00,670
This is a two-way street.

402
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:04,630
Really?

403
00:19:06,070 --> 00:19:07,160
Really.

404
00:19:07,210 --> 00:19:10,140
Now this all better be here when I come back.

405
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:13,610
Yeah, of course. I can control myself.

406
00:19:26,310 --> 00:19:28,220
Stop staring at me!

407
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:42,040
Just a tiny little....

408
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,830
I'm not even sorry.

409
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:04,710
- Hi.  - Hey.

410
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:09,180
So these are the preliminary forms for an open adoption.

411
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:10,600
There's a lot to go over,

412
00:20:10,650 --> 00:20:12,520
but I'll explain as we go through.

413
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,770
- Is that a picture? - Yeah.

414
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:19,410
It's a sonogram they took of the baby last week.

415
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:21,280
I thought you might want to see it.

416
00:20:28,490 --> 00:20:30,270
Look, doctor.

417
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,210
Look, before we sign anything,

418
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:38,090
we really have to talk.

419
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:43,510
We're not who you think we are.

420
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,920
I don't understand.

421
00:20:44,970 --> 00:20:46,760
The agency must have made a mistake.

422
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:48,020
My wife is not a reverend,

423
00:20:48,070 --> 00:20:49,660
and I'm not a doctor.

424
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:51,760
- What? - That's impossible.

425
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,480
I could perform an operation on you

426
00:20:53,530 --> 00:20:55,010
and prove it if you'd like.

427
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:59,700
I have to check your file. Excuse me.

428
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:01,650
So who are you?

429
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:05,240
Our names really are Monica and Chandler. We're from New York.

430
00:21:05,290 --> 00:21:07,510
Yeah, but the important thing to know about us...

431
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:11,080
...is how much we would care for this little baby.

432
00:21:11,130 --> 00:21:13,290
So you lied to me before?

433
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:16,840
Well, we "bore false witness."

434
00:21:18,150 --> 00:21:20,220
See? I could be a reverend.

435
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,320
I can't believe this.

436
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:25,930
But we were hoping that since we told you the truth...

437
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:27,580
...that you still might consider--

438
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:29,430
Giving you my baby?

439
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:31,890
You think I'd give you my child after this?

440
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:33,020
You don't have to decide now.

441
00:21:33,070 --> 00:21:34,590
If you look at our file--

442
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:37,240
I don't want to look at your file. This is over.

443
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:43,560
Erica, wait.

444
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:45,930
I have nothing to say to you.

445
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:48,310
Look, you have every reason to be upset.

446
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:49,950
We did lie.

447
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,690
But only because we've been waiting

448
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:54,390
and trying to have a baby for so long.

449
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:56,140
And we don't know how long it's gonna be

450
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:57,820
before we get another chance again.

451
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:00,120
Why don't you ask the reverend to pray on it?

452
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:03,100
Erica, please.

453
00:22:03,150 --> 00:22:05,240
Just consider us.

454
00:22:05,290 --> 00:22:07,210
Ask them to see our file.

455
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,670
Our last name's Bing.

456
00:22:09,790 --> 00:22:12,430
My wife's a chef, and I'm in advertising.

457
00:22:13,670 --> 00:22:15,020
Oh, yeah.

458
00:22:15,750 --> 00:22:17,650
I actually liked you guys.

459
00:22:19,470 --> 00:22:20,490
But it doesn't matter.

460
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:21,780
Because what you did was wrong.

461
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:23,940
But you did like us.

462
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,320
And you should.

463
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:29,300
My wife's an incredible woman.

464
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:33,340
She is loving, and devoted and caring.

465
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:35,730
And don't tell her I said this,

466
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:37,420
but the woman's always right.

467
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:44,750
I love my wife more than anything in this world.

468
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,810
And it...

469
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:52,210
It kills me that I can't give her a baby.

470
00:22:58,110 --> 00:22:59,980
I really want a kid.

471
00:23:01,530 --> 00:23:02,800
And when that day finally comes,

472
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,860
I'll learn how to be a good dad.

473
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:07,160
But my wife...

474
00:23:07,910 --> 00:23:09,860
...she's already there.

475
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,110
She's a mother...

476
00:23:13,490 --> 00:23:15,270
...without a baby.

477
00:23:22,870 --> 00:23:24,400
Please?

478
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:38,230
You still want that baby?

479
00:23:54,210 --> 00:23:56,620
God bless you, Chandler Bing!

480
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:13,310
Turns out this sweater is made for a woman.

481
00:24:15,290 --> 00:24:17,140
So why are you still wearing it?

482
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:18,770
Because it's soft.

483
00:24:20,590 --> 00:24:22,620
Hey, so how was your date?

484
00:24:22,620 --> 00:24:23,890
Not so good.

485
00:24:26,470 --> 00:24:29,550
Well, looks like it's just the two of us tonight,

486
00:24:29,550 --> 00:24:30,610
huh, buddy?

487
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:32,680
Yeah. And you know what?

488
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:34,090
We could do a lot worse.

489
00:24:34,090 --> 00:24:35,720
- Yeah. - Yeah.

490
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:41,930
Joey doesn't share food!

